  "instructionButton": "GUIDE",
  "instructionTitle": "How it works",
  "instructionPhilosophy": "IronVibe deliberately ships without a built-in exercise catalog or preset \"programs.\" It is not here to teach you how to train—YouTube and real coaches already do that—but to help you keep stats exactly the way you like. You type exercise names yourself, in your own words. Optionally tag a muscle group so the app can assemble a quick full-body session from your own list. The longer you use it, the more it feels like home: the app learns your habits and adapts to you, not the other way around.",
  "instructionSectionSetControl": "Set controls",
  "instructionSetMinusLabel": "Minus",
  "instructionSetMinusDesc": "Removes the last set. If that row already has weight, reps, or RIR, the app asks for confirmation. An empty row is removed right away. If only one set remains: in the current workout the row is cleared; in saved history the whole exercise is deleted.",
  "instructionSetPlusLabel": "Plus",
  "instructionSetPlusDesc": "Adds a new empty set row to this exercise.",
  "instructionSetProgressLabel": "Timeline",
  "instructionSetProgressDesc": "Opens the progress timeline for this exercise.",
  "instructionSectionProgressChart": "Progress chart",
  "instructionProgressChartIntro": "Three independent trends by date: red — heaviest single set that day; cyan — most reps in any single set that day; yellow — exercise volume (sum of weight × reps for that day). Left axis: weight; right axis: reps; yellow is shown as a normalized trend.",
  "instructionProgressLineWeightLabel": "Weight",
  "instructionProgressLineWeightDesc": "Red line: maximum weight in one set on each calendar day.",
  "instructionProgressLineRepsLabel": "Reps",
  "instructionProgressLineRepsDesc": "Cyan line: maximum reps in one set that day (not tied to the heaviest weight).",
  "instructionProgressLineVolumeDesc": "Yellow line: daily exercise volume (tonnage), calculated as the sum of weight × reps for sets where both values are logged.",
  "instructionProgressChartSessionHighlight": "During an active workout, the chart button under the sets may tint in the same colors as the graph: red if you beat your previous best weight in a single set; yellow if total exercise volume beats your past best for that movement; cyan if the exercise is bodyweight-only and your total reps (sum across all sets) beat your past best. If several apply, priority is red, then yellow, then cyan. The tint appears only while you are logging the current workout—not in saved history.",
  "instructionSectionWorkout": "Workout",
  "instructionAddExerciseTitle": "Add exercise",
  "instructionAddExerciseBody": "Adds a new block. Name the current exercise first — the app will remind you if that field is still empty.",
  "instructionSectionExerciseNameTools": "Exercise name",
  "instructionRenameExerciseTitle": "Long press to rename",
  "instructionRenameExerciseDesc": "Long-press the exercise name while logging a workout, on a suggestion in the dropdown, or on the title in a saved workout in history to rename that exercise everywhere.",
  "instructionRemoveFromBankTitle": "Remove from your list",
  "instructionRemoveFromBankDesc": "When the suggestions list is open under the name field, tap the X on a row — or the red X in Personal Progress — to remove that name from suggestions and the progress table. Saved workouts stay unchanged.",
  "instructionSectionInputs": "Data fields",
  "instructionWeightTitle": "Weight",
  "instructionWeightBody": "Load on the bar or equipment. Type the number in kg or lb — whichever you use. The app does not convert units.",
  "instructionRepsTitle": "Reps",
  "instructionRepsBody": "How many times you completed the movement in one set.",
  "instructionRirTitle": "RIR",
  "instructionRirBody": "How many more reps you could still do before failure. Helps track intensity.",
  "instructionOneRmTitle": "1RM (one-rep max)",
  "instructionOneRmDesc": "Estimated maximum weight for one full repetition from your current weight and reps. A key strength benchmark for tracking progress and picking working weights.",
  "instructionExerciseVolumeTitle": "Exercise volume (total)",
  "instructionExerciseVolumeDesc": "Next to the progress (chart) button under the sets: total tonnage for this exercise—the sum of weight × reps for every set that has both values. Updates live as you add or edit sets.",
  "instructionSectionPersonalProgress": "Personal progress",
  "instructionPersonalProgressIntro": "One table of every movement from saved workouts: best set, estimated 1RM, and max volume. Search to find a name. Star favorites; tap the small chip under the name to tag a muscle group; the red X removes the name from suggestions and this table (saved workouts stay). Open it from your training menu or a client profile.",
  "instructionSectionSaving": "Saving",
  "instructionFinishTitle": "Finish workout",
  "instructionFinishBody": "Confirms and writes the session to history. If you leave earlier, you can save, discard, or stay. A draft is also kept automatically if the app is interrupted.",
  "instructionSectionCardio": "Cardio & intensity",
  "instructionCardioTitle": "Cardio",
  "instructionCardioBody": "Tracks time and intensity for cardio (distance is not entered). Helps you keep pace and monitor effort.",
  "instructionIntensityTitle": "Intensity",
  "instructionIntensityBody": "Use the effort scale to gauge how hard the workout felt. That is the key to progress without overtraining.",
  "instructionSectionStopwatch": "Stopwatch (your assistant)",
  "instructionStopwatchWhyTitle": "Why use it?",
  "instructionStopwatchWhyBody": "To control rest between sets. Short rest — higher density; long rest — more strength for heavy weight.",
  "instructionStopwatchHowTitle": "How does it work?",
  "instructionStopwatchHowBody": "Center: time, Play/Pause, and Reset. Left and right: quick presets (below). In plain stopwatch mode time runs up with centiseconds. The timer stays pinned in the header while you scroll.",
  "instructionStopwatchIntervalsTitle": "Left: intervals",
  "instructionStopwatchIntervalsBody": "1/1 — 60 s work, 60 s rest. 4/4 — 4 minutes work and 4 minutes rest each round. 20/10 — Tabata-style: 20 s on, 10 s off. After you pick one, the timer loops work and rest until you pause or reset. Red tint means work; blue means rest.",
  "instructionStopwatchRestTitle": "Right: rest countdown",
  "instructionStopwatchRestBody": "+1m, +2m, and +5m start or extend a normal minute countdown. If an interval loop was running, it switches to this countdown. If a countdown is already running, the minutes are added to the time left. Handy for rest between sets.",
  "instructionStopwatchProgressTitle": "Progress bar",
  "instructionStopwatchProgressBody": "During countdown and interval modes, a bar under the time shows how much of the current phase remains.",
  "instructionStopwatchSoundsTitle": "Sound & haptics",
  "instructionStopwatchSoundsBody": "At 3, 2, and 1 seconds left in a phase, a short in-app sound and light haptic play. When the phase ends or work/rest switches, a stronger cue and haptic follow. Sounds are minimal bundled clips—no microphone, no notification permission; media/system volume still affects loudness.",
  "instructionSectionNavHistory": "History & data",
  "instructionNavHistoryTitle": "History / statistics",
  "instructionNavHistoryDesc": "In calendar/history each workout shows total tonnage. Workout volume is one of the best indicators of hypertrophy: the more quality volume you accumulate, the more muscle you can build.",
  "instructionNavImportExportTitle": "Import / export",
  "instructionNavImportExportDesc": "Back up or transfer your data using JSON export and import in the statistics dialog. Backups include workout history, your exercise list, favorites, and muscle-group tags. Coach backups are separate from personal history. A coach can also import an athlete's history as a new client without mixing exercise names.",
  "instructionSectionHome": "Home",
  "instructionThemeTitle": "Theme",
  "instructionThemeDesc": "The sun / moon switch on the home screen toggles light and dark. Your choice is remembered.",
  "instructionTrainSelfTitle": "I train myself",
  "instructionTrainSelfDesc": "Your own workouts, calendar, personal progress, favorites, a rhythm gauge of how often you train, and a full-body quick workout built from your tagged exercises.",
  "instructionTrainOthersTitle": "I train others",
  "instructionTrainOthersDesc": "Coach mode: clients, a schedule, and a separate history per person. Each client has their own progress table and favorites.",
  "instructionSectionAthleteMenu": "Your training",
  "instructionStartWorkoutTitle": "Start workout",
  "instructionStartWorkoutDesc": "Opens an empty session — it does not copy the last workout. Add exercises, log sets, then finish to save.",
  "instructionQuickWorkoutTitle": "Quick workout",
  "instructionQuickWorkoutDesc": "Assembles a 4-exercise full-body session: chest, back, one leg movement (front or rear thigh — never both), and one accessory for shoulders, arms, or core, whichever you have trained least recently. Prefers favorites. Last weights and reps appear greyed as a target to beat — you log each set yourself.",
  "instructionCalendarMenuTitle": "Workout calendar",
  "instructionCalendarMenuDesc": "See which days you trained, open a saved session, or add a workout on a chosen date and time — including past days.",
  "instructionPersonalProgressMenuDesc": "A table of your best sets, estimated 1RM, and max volume. Star favorites and tag muscle groups here.",
  "instructionFavoritesMenuTitle": "Favorite exercises",
  "instructionFavoritesMenuDesc": "Your starred list. Tick the ones you want and tap Build workout to start a session in that order. Last weights and reps appear greyed as a target to beat.",
  "instructionSectionRhythm": "Training rhythm",
  "instructionRhythmIntro": "After a few strength sessions, a gauge appears at the top of your training screen. It shows how many days per week you have trained on average over the last four weeks. Cardio-only days are not counted. The number is a snapshot of your density — not a target the app expects you to hit. Tap it for a note about your pace and what an active recovery week can look like.",
  "instructionRhythmGaugeTitle": "Days per week",
  "instructionRhythmGaugeDesc": "The arc fills from 1 to 6 days per week. Color moves from steel through gold toward rust as density rises. The gauge appears once you have at least three strength days in that four-week window.",
  "instructionRhythmDeloadTitle": "Active recovery week reminder",
  "instructionRhythmDeloadDesc": "If you have been training about two and a half days a week or more for several weeks without an active recovery week, the app may remind you that a short active recovery week is sometimes useful — about 30% less tonnage and reps. The more days per week, the sooner that reminder. It is a reminder, not a prescription. You will see it at most once per week, and only in your own training mode — not automatically for clients. Tap a client's gauge for the same note.",
  "instructionSectionFavorites": "Favorites",
  "instructionFavoriteStarTitle": "Star",
  "instructionFavoriteStarDesc": "In Personal Progress, tap the star next to an exercise to add or remove it from favorites. Favorites stay at the top of the table.",
  "instructionBuildFromFavoritesTitle": "Build workout",
  "instructionBuildFromFavoritesDesc": "On the favorites screen, tick the exercises you want. The button appears when at least one is selected. Last weights and reps appear greyed as a target to beat — you log each set yourself. For a client, the same action starts a session for that person.",
  "instructionSectionMuscleGroups": "Muscle groups & quick workout",
  "instructionMuscleGroupsIntro": "Groups are optional labels you attach to your own exercise names. They are not a catalog: they only help Quick workout pick a balanced full-body mix. Eight groups: chest, back, shoulders, core, front thigh, rear thigh, arm curl, arm extension.",
  "instructionMuscleGroupTagTitle": "How to tag",
  "instructionMuscleGroupTagDesc": "When you first enter a new exercise name, the app asks for a group. You can skip with Later, or mark Not for quick workout if you do not want that movement in a full-body mix. Tap the small chip under the name in Personal Progress or Favorites to change or clear it.",
  "instructionQuickWorkoutHowTitle": "How a quick session is built",
  "instructionQuickWorkoutHowDesc": "Four slots: chest, back, one half of the legs, then shoulders/arms/core by recency. A preview lets you swap any slot for another exercise in the same group. Add more yourself if you want a longer session.",
  "instructionStrengthCardioTitle": "Strength / Cardio",
  "instructionStrengthCardioDesc": "Switch at the top of the session. Strength: weight, reps, RIR. Cardio: time and intensity only — no distance field.",
  "instructionPreviousHintsTitle": "Grey last-session numbers",
  "instructionPreviousHintsDesc": "When you pick an exercise in a client session, a quick workout, or a session built from favorites, last logged weights and reps show as grey placeholders — a minimum to beat, not a finished set. Only numbers you type are saved to history.",
  "instructionRemoveExerciseTitle": "Remove from this workout",
  "instructionRemoveExerciseDesc": "Removes that block from the current session only. Saved history is not affected until you finish.",
  "instructionReassignExerciseTitle": "Change exercise in history",
  "instructionReassignExerciseDesc": "In a saved workout you can reassign a block to a different name. Only that session changes; charts follow the new name. Sets stay as they were.",
  "instructionAutoSaveTitle": "Interrupted workout",
  "instructionAutoSaveDesc": "If the app closes mid-session, it offers to continue where you left off or delete the unsaved draft.",
  "instructionSectionCalendar": "Calendar",
  "instructionCalendarAddTitle": "Add on a date",
  "instructionCalendarAddDesc": "Pick a day, then add a workout at a chosen time. Useful for logging a missed session.",
  "instructionSectionTrainer": "Coach mode",
  "instructionTrainerIntro": "I train others is for coaches. Add clients, schedule sessions, plan exercises ahead of time, and log workouts per person. Repeating the last session is optional. Export and import for coach data is separate from your personal history. Deleting a client removes future sessions but keeps past workouts for reporting.",
  "instructionClientsTitle": "Clients",
  "instructionClientsDesc": "Add, edit, or delete clients. The list shows the last and next session. Profile fields: goal, weight, height, and private coach notes.",
  "instructionClientProfileTitle": "Client profile",
  "instructionClientProfileDesc": "Start today's session from the profile: an empty live workout. Grey last-session numbers appear only after you pick an exercise. History lists completed workouts only. Plan future sessions on the calendar. Progress and favorites are on the same screen. When there is enough recent strength work, a rhythm gauge shows how often they train; tap it for a note about pace and rest. Unsaved profile edits ask before you leave.",
  "instructionTrainerPlanTitle": "Plan a session",
  "instructionTrainerPlanDesc": "Plan only from the coach calendar: pick a client and date, then name exercises. Previous weights and reps appear grey as a hint. A planned session shows a play icon. Tap it to start (today) or delete. Only finished workouts go to history. A plan whose date has already passed is removed.",
  "instructionTrainerRepeatTitle": "Repeat last workout",
  "instructionTrainerRepeatDesc": "Optional. From the client profile, or as a switch when adding a session on the calendar. Copies the last session's exercises into today's live workout or a new plan; previous weights and reps show as grey hints, not as finished sets.",
  "printSession": "Print",
  "printSessionEmpty": "Nothing to print yet. Log at least one set.",
  "printSessionShareText": "IronVibe session",
  "instructionPrintSessionTitle": "Print a session",
  "instructionPrintSessionDesc": "On a finished client workout, the print icon in the header makes an A4 sheet of that day as logged. Share, save, or print from the system sheet.",
  "rhythmPerWeek": "per week",
  "deloadNudgeTitle": "An active recovery week?",
  "deloadNudgeBody": "You've been training about {rate} days a week for roughly {weeks} weeks. This is a reminder that a short active recovery week is sometimes useful — about 30% less tonnage and reps. Not a prescription.",
